          "description": {
            "comment": "The wrinkle-faced bat (Centurio senex) is a species of bat in the family Phyllostomidae found in various countries in and around Central America (from Wikipedia entry). This sample of a female individual found in Lamanai, Belize was procured by Nancy Simmons to generate a high-quality genome for the Bat1K project and the Bat Biology Foundation. Sequencing was conducted at Paratus Sciences and genome assembly at the Vertebrate Genome Lab (VGL) of the Rockefeller University, led by Erich Jarvis, Giulio Formenti, and Jennifer Balacco. Use of this data is limited under embargo until the publication of the manuscript \"Reference genomes and fossils rewrite bat family- level phylogeny and global biogeography\" (Morales et al.).",
